## Context

Three gaps that would cause an agent to make mistakes when using only the manual:

1. **Blocked-by format not defined.** The manual references "local-ref (NNNN)" and
   "forge-ref (host/owner/repo#N)" but never gives the grammar. An agent must know
   to read spec-erg-v1.md. At minimum, a one-line syntax summary should appear in
   the `erg validate` or `erg close` section.

2. **`erg archive` top-level scope ambiguous.** "Scans the top-level of DIR" could
   mean DIR root only, or recursively. Clarify: only direct children of DIR are
   considered (not tickets already in subdirectories like closed/).

3. **`erg close` step 3 edge cases absent.** Missing: behaviour when the same ID
   appears in multiple Blocked-by lines of one ticket; what happens to already-closed
   tickets that reference the closed ID; atomicity on partial failure.

## Actions
1. In `erg validate` helpText, add a one-line Blocked-by grammar summary.
2. In `erg archive` helpText, replace "top-level" with explicit wording.
3. In `erg close` helpText step 3, add one sentence on multi-ref and idempotency.
4. Run `make test && make docs`.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Blocked-by grammar inline or referenced in manual
- [ ] `erg archive` scope unambiguous
- [ ] `erg close` step 3 edge cases addressed
- [ ] `make test` passes
